      "synonyms": [],
      "props": {
        "title": "Mock Paper One: a placeholder cohort of Mock Disease One",
        "abstract": "Mock abstract for Mock Paper One. This placeholder study describes a mock cohort of twelve\nindividuals with Mock Disease One. In this mock cohort, gain-of-function changes in Mock Gene A\nwere present in every individual with Mock Disease One. In mock cell assays, Mock Variant A1\nincreased signalling through Mock Pathway Alpha compared with the reference sequence, and the\nincrease was larger than for other mock variants of Mock Gene A. In a mock case series of six\ntreated individuals, Mock Drug X was followed by fewer episodes of Mock Phenotype P. Every name,\nnumber and finding in this abstract is a placeholder and describes no real study.",
        "year": 2000,
        "journal": "Mock Journal of Placeholder Studies",
        "authors": [
          "Mock Investigator One",
          "Mock Investigator Two"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "mock:paper:2",
      "type": "Paper",
      "label": "Mock Paper Two",
      "synonyms": [],
      "props": {
        "title": "Mock Paper Two: a placeholder treatment report",
        "abstract": "Mock abstract for Mock Paper Two. This placeholder report describes seven mock individuals with\nMock Disease One: four who received Mock Drug X and three who received Mock Drug Y.  Mock Drug X\ndid not reduce the frequency of Mock Phenotype P in the four mock individuals who received it.\nMock Drug Y was followed by fewer episodes of Mock Phenotype Q in all three mock individuals who\nreceived it. Every statement in this abstract is a placeholder and describes no real study.",
        "year": 2001,
        "journal": "Mock Journal of Placeholder Studies",
        "authors": [
